  "revision_notes": [
    "Corrected preview lighting and palette",
    "Added a root node per decoration asset",
    "Fixed duplicate parenting translations",
    "Grounded all asset pivots",
    "Excluded inherited reference objects from preview",
    "Fitted camera to all nine assets",
    "Horizontal deadwood with a flat support band",
    "Irregular single-body rock silhouettes",
    "Fine 44-blade gravel grass",
    "Branching shrubs with separate folded leaves",
    "Replaced sparse shrub twigs with overlapping irregular foliage crowns and short woody bases",
    "Included the original three soil grasses and arranged twelve same-scale decoration samples",
    "Scaled both cacti and deadwood by 0.7, both shrubs and all three stones by 0.8; preserved all four grasses",
    "Added one low-poly open scallop shell, one algae-faceted underwater stone, and one ribbon-leaf seagrass tuft; preserved existing twelve assets and did not place decorations on terrain",
    "Replaced fan shell with oval clam, crystalline stone with rounded waterworn pebble, and straight grass with broad S-curved kelp ribbons; preserved other twelve assets.",
    "Uniformly scaled only underwater shell and stone to 70 percent; preserved seaweed, all land decorations, gallery positions, and grounded pivots.",
    "Scaled only the underwater stone by another 0.7, reaching 0.49 of its initial size; shell, seaweed, other decorations, and gallery positions unchanged.",
    "Added four unapproved low-poly samples: humid-sand bunchgrass, humid-soil willow and broadleaf tree, humid-rock fern; preserved all fifteen approved assets and did not change terrain or active placement rules.",
    "Replaced only the wet-sand cattail-like grass with a round tumbleweed and the damp-rock leafy spray with paired-pinnule fern fronds; two wet-soil trees and fifteen original assets unchanged.",
    "Revised the two models against the user's references: upward-curving rooted tumbleweed and compact crevice fern with paired rounded pinnae; other seventeen assets preserved.",
    "Rebuilt tumbleweed branches to spread outward near the root, rise along the perimeter and curl inward; flattened fern fronds to creep over the stone surface.",
    "Added eighteen fine inner tumbleweed stems and eighteen forks without changing its outer branches; varied fern frond directions, lengths, sideways bends and low heights to remove the hexagonal radial pattern.",
    "Redesigned the three soil grass types as a short dense tuft, taller arching blades, and a short tuft with two small ivory wildflowers; preserved the sixteen other assets.",
    "Reduced short, tall and flowering grass to 4, 9 and 7 cm; separated white petals and yellow centers into independent single-material meshes; verified the exported GLB after import and rendered that actual file.",
    "Scaled both wet-soil trees to 0.5 of the previous size, and tumbleweed and creeping rock fern to 0.7; preserved all gallery positions and other fifteen assets.",
    "Scaled both wet-soil trees to 0.7 and tumbleweed to 0.8 of their current size; preserved all gallery positions, the creeping rock fern and the other fifteen assets.",
    "Moved tumbleweed, willow, broadleaf tree and creeping rock fern into a fourth column alongside the original twelve land decorations; retained all accepted sizes and underwater assets.",
    "Darkened only tumbleweed branches and seed bracts to brown, and lowered its geometry 0.02 m relative to its placement pivot; retained all model sizes and gallery positions.",
    "Added lotus leaves, sweet flag and reeds in a fifth column beside the existing nineteen accepted decorations; retained existing geometry, sizes and positions.",
    "Revised lotus using embedded vein albedo; reused exact early wet-sand grass for sweet flag; rebuilt fuller beige reed panicles and baked all river-plant colors into a single atlas per mesh.",
    "User approved river-plant appearance; scaled lotus to 0.7, sweet flag and reeds to 0.5 of their preceding size, preserving root pivots and gallery positions.",
    "Enlarged the accepted reed by 1.2 from its preceding size, to 0.6 of its original geometry.",
    "Consolidated natural assets into single meshes with one shared palette material; preserved original river leaf-vein UVs, geometry, gallery positions and grounded pivots. Grass patches are unchanged."
  ],
